---
import FutureTechMissionFrame from '../../../../components/FutureTechMissionFrame.astro';
---
<FutureTechMissionFrame
  missionNumber="1"
  title="Make It Happen"
  tagline="Code your first micro:bit and make it respond to you."
  question="How can I give a tiny computer instructions and make it respond to me?"
  success="I can create code, run it on a micro:bit, make it respond to an input, and explain what my code is doing."
  nextTitle="Mission 2 — Make It Think"
  nextHref="../mission-2-make-it-think/"
>
  <section id="stage-1" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">01</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">GET READY</p><h2 class="stage-title">Set Up</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Grab your tools, find the four parts you will use today, and make sure your station is ready.</p>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Computer</span><span>☐ micro:bit</span><span>☐ USB data cable</span><span>☐ Mission page open</span></div>
    <p class="concept">Find these four parts: Button A · Button B · 5×5 LED display · USB port.</p>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Button A + Button B</strong><p>These are <b>inputs</b>. You press them to give information to the program.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>LED display</strong><p>This is an <b>output</b>. Your program can make it show images, numbers, and words.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="mini-label">Maker rules</p>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Handle equipment carefully</span><span>☐ Keep food and drinks away</span><span>☐ Never force a connection</span><span>☐ Return everything when finished</span></div>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-2" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">02</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">FIRST SUCCESS</p><h2 class="stage-title">First Code</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Create a tiny program, test it on screen, then send it to the real micro:bit.</p>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><strong>1 — Open MakeCode</strong><p>Open <a class="external" href="https://makecode.microbit.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MakeCode for micro:bit ↗</a>. Choose <b>New Project</b>. Name it <code>FirstName_L1_M1</code>.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>2 — Make your first program</strong><p>Put <code>show string</code> inside <code>on start</code>. Type your initials.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>3 — Test the simulator</strong><p>Your initials should scroll across the virtual micro:bit on screen.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>4 — Run it for real</strong><p>Connect the micro:bit with USB. Click <b>Download</b> and send the newest program to the device.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="success">✓ Success looks like this: your initials scroll across the real micro:bit.</p>
    <p class="warning">If it does not work: check the cable, test the simulator, then download the newest version again.</p>
    <p class="concept">Mini Check: point to the <b>output</b>. The LED display is the output because it shows the result of the program.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-3" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">03</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">INPUT → CODE → OUTPUT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Make It React</h2></div></div>
    <div class="route"><span>INPUT: Button</span><span>CODE: Event</span><span>OUTPUT: LED display</span></div>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge A — Button A</strong><p>Add <code>on button A pressed</code>. Put <code>show icon</code> inside it. Pick any icon.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge B — Button B</strong><p>Add <code>on button B pressed</code>. Make it show something different.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge C — Sequence</strong><p>Make one button run at least three instructions. Example: image → pause → image.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>What is a sequence?</strong><p>A <b>sequence</b> is a set of instructions happening in order.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="success">✓ Before moving on: test A, test B, and run the program on the physical micro:bit.</p>
    <p class="warning">If an animation changes too fast, add a pause between images.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-4" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">04</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">YOUR CREATION</p><h2 class="stage-title">Build It — Interactive Badge</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Create a digital badge that tells us something about you. It must react differently to Button A and Button B.</p>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Button A works</span><span>☐ Button B works</span><span>☐ The responses are different</span><span>☐ One response uses a sequence</span><span>☐ It runs on the real micro:bit</span><span>☐ You changed it to make it yours</span></div>
    <p class="mini-label">Need an idea?</p>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Idea 1</strong><p>A = favourite activity · B = initials + animation.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Idea 2</strong><p>A = happy face · B = favourite number.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="try4"><strong>STUCK? TRY 4</strong><p>1. CHECK your blocks. 2. SIMULATE the newest code. 3. DOWNLOAD the newest version. 4. PARTNER — explain what should happen. Still stuck? Ask for help and say what you already tried.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-5" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">05</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">OPTIONAL CHALLENGE</p><h2 class="stage-title">Level It Up</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Only after Build It works. Choose one while you wait for your checkpoint.</p>
    <div class="level-grid">
      <article class="level-card"><strong>Shake It</strong><p>Make shaking the micro:bit trigger an output.</p></article>
      <article class="level-card"><strong>A + B</strong><p>Add a third response when A and B are pressed together.</p></article>
      <article class="level-card"><strong>Animator</strong><p>Create an animation with at least five frames.</p></article>
      <article class="level-card"><strong>Explorer</strong><p>Find another MakeCode input and make it work.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="success">When every Build It box is checked, add your name or pair to the Ready-for-Check queue. Keep Leveling Up until you are called.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-6" class="stage checkpoint">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">06</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SHOW WHAT YOU KNOW</p><h2 class="stage-title">Checkpoint</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Bring your micro:bit and open your code when you are called. Each student completes the checkpoint individually.</p>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Check 1 — Make It Work</strong><p>Press A or B. Identify the <b>input</b> and the <b>output</b>.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Check 2 — Explain It</strong><p>Point to one event. Explain what makes that code run.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Check 3 — Change It</strong><p>Make one small change chosen by the teacher. Test the new version.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>After Your Check</strong><p><b>PASS</b> = Mission Complete. <b>NOT YET</b> = fix one skill and retry.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage passport">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">✓</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SKILL PASSPORT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Mission 1 Skills</h2></div></div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ I can run code on a micro:bit</span><span>☐ I can use an input</span><span>☐ I can create an output</span><span>☐ I can use an event and sequence</span><span>☐ I can change and test my code</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage reset">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">↺</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">LEAVE IT READY</p><h2 class="stage-title">Reset</h2></div></div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Project saved correctly</span><span>☐ micro:bit back in the numbered kit</span><span>☐ USB cable loosely coiled</span><span>☐ Kit complete and workspace clear</span><span>☐ Damage or missing equipment reported</span></div>
    <p class="concept">Exit question: What is one thing you made the micro:bit do today?</p>
  </section>
</FutureTechMissionFrame>
